# Ülke paritesi — Türkiye’de yapılan, altı ülkede de yapılır

**Read and follow** `.cursor/skills/ulke-paritesi-duzeltme/SKILL.md` before closing any change that touches the Turkish doctor product.

Boss rule (Kaan, 2026-10-18): any change made in Türkiye is applied to **us, gb, ca, au, nz, uz** in the **same change**. No exceptions. No “next PR”. No OPEN-COMMITMENTS substitute. Logging a gap does not finish the work.

Each country gets that change in **its own** language and under **its own** rules, regulations, government, and medical-institution directives. Do not paste Turkish copy, Turkish identifiers, or Turkish institutions (SGK, Medula, e-Nabız, KVKK, NVI, GİB) into another country. Build that country’s equivalent from that country’s own authorities.

1. Core doctor behavior is already 1:1 across the 30 branches and the 10 Özel Branşlar (`.cursor/rules/ortak-omurga-paritesi.mdc`). Inside every country, that same 1:1 holds.
2. A specialty-only screen stays in that specialty, and that specialty’s version in each country is sourced from that country. It does not leak into the other specialties.
3. The commit/PR report has one status line per country saying what landed there and which authority the local wording follows.
4. `main` does not contain `countries/`. Country builds are `release/<cc>`. A fix on `main` has not reached a country until that branch has the adapted change. Do not check a release branch out into this worktree; port it in its own worktree.
